---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SeamRail from '../components/SeamRail.astro';
import BrandDevice from '../components/BrandDevice.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Approach"
  description="The Think / Say / Do method, the five-stage delivery journey, and the evidence discipline behind every InclusionEdge engagement."
>
  <section class="page-hero surface-navy">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Approach</span>
      <h1>One method, running the whole way through.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A framework is only useful if it survives contact with delivery. Ours is built as a single
        method — Think, Say, Do — that threads every tier, every stage of an engagement, and every
        artefact we hand over.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Think Say Do -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The method</span>
        <h2>Think / Say / Do</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Every module at every tier is built through the same three-part lens. It is what stops
          CARE, ENGAGE and ENABLE becoming three programmes with three vocabularies.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="method-card">
          <span class="method-label">Think</span>
          <h3>The cognitive shift</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Noticing an assumption before it hardens into a reaction. This is where CARE&rsquo;s
            &ldquo;Consider&rdquo; lives — the deliberate pause that makes everything after it
            possible.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <span class="method-label">Say</span>
          <h3>Scripting for the supporter</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            What the colleague, manager or leader actually says in the moment a need surfaces. Not
            a script for the person being supported — the burden of translation has sat with them
            for long enough.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="method-card">
          <span class="method-label">Do</span>
          <h3>Observable action</h3>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The change that follows, defaulting to universal design wherever possible — so support
            improves the work for everyone in the role, rather than singling anyone out.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="pull-quote">
        &ldquo;Say&rdquo; is not a script for the person being accommodated to perform. It is what
        the supporter learns to say.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Programme spine -->
  <section class="section surface-tint">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="spine">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">The programme spine</span>
          <h2>Invisible differences, with neurodivergence as the deep case.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Every tier is taught through one connected spine rather than a rotating set of
            unconnected diversity topics.
          </p>
          <p>
            Neurodivergence is the deep teaching case because it is where the gap between stated
            intent and lived reality is widest, and where the resulting behaviours transfer most
            broadly. A manager who learns to handle ambiguity in instruction-giving for a
            neurodivergent colleague has learned something that applies to a new joiner, a
            returning parent, and a team member working across a language difference.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="spine-layers">
          <div class="layer layer-deep">
            <span class="layer-tag">Deep dive</span>
            <h3>Neurodivergence at work</h3>
            <p class="text-small text-muted">
              Full scenario banks, case illustration and behavioural practice, built around this
              teaching case and then extended outward.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="layer">
            <span class="layer-tag">Reconnect layer</span>
            <h3>Life stage &amp; intergenerational</h3>
            <p class="text-small text-muted">
              Connected back to the same CARE behaviours rather than taught as a separate module.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="layer">
            <span class="layer-tag">Reconnect layer</span>
            <h3>Mental health &amp; wellbeing</h3>
            <p class="text-small text-muted">
              Same behavioural core, applied where disclosure and support boundaries need care.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- The journey / seam rail -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The journey</span>
        <h2>What you see. What runs underneath.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A single practice delivers at team depth because the infrastructure between client
          touchpoints is AI-first. We show the seam deliberately — how the proof gets built is part
          of the proof.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="rail-legend">
        <span><i class="dot dot-visible" aria-hidden="true"></i>What you experience directly</span>
        <span><i class="dot dot-seam" aria-hidden="true"></i>What runs in the seam</span>
      </div>

      <SeamRail />
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Evidence discipline (folded in) -->
  <section class="section surface-navy">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="evidence">
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow">Evidence discipline</span>
          <h2>Unverified means unpublished.</h2>
          <p class="lede">
            Widely-cited inclusion and neurodiversity statistics are frequently garbled, stripped of
            context, or specific to a role or region by the time they reach a slide. Where a claim
            cannot be traced to its original source, we leave it out — not approximated, not
            rounded, not &ldquo;generally understood to be true.&rdquo;
          </p>
          <p class="lede">
            An empty evidence slot is the discipline working, not a gap in the deck. Measurement
            follows the same rule: a short pilot does not get to claim causal return on investment,
            and where a result could plausibly have other causes, we say so.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="evidence-panel">
          <h3>Sources we work from</h3>
          <ul class="source-list">
            <li>
              <strong>Dobbin &amp; Kalev</strong>
              <span>Multi-decade study of workplace diversity practice across several hundred organisations.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>SG Enable</strong>
              <span>Singapore employment support data and the Enabling Skills and Competencies Framework.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Enabling Masterplan 2030</strong>
              <span>National direction on disability inclusion and employment participation.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Workplace Fairness Act</strong>
              <span>Statutory protection against workplace discrimination, ahead of its implementation date.</span>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Kirkpatrick evaluation model</strong>
              <span>Measurement weighted toward Levels 3 and 4 — behaviour and results.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-sm cta-band">
    <div class="container cta-inner">
      <BrandDevice variant="seam" class="cta-device" />
      <h2>See the method as working instruments.</h2>
      <p class="lede">
        The showcase holds the actual diagnostic and measurement artefacts, not descriptions of
        them.
      </p>
      <a href="/showcase/" class="btn btn-primary">Open the showcase</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-hero { padding-block: clamp(4rem, 8vw, 6.5rem); }
  .page-hero h1 { max-width: 18ch; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  .page-hero .lede { max-width: 56ch; }

  .method-card {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--navy);
    padding-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .method-label {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--teal-deep);
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
  }

  .method-card h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.7rem; }
  .method-card p { font-size: 0.92rem; margin: 0; }

  .spine {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .spine h2 { margin-bottom: 1.15rem; }
  .spine .lede { margin-bottom: 1.15rem; }

  .spine-layers { display: grid; gap: 1rem; }

  .layer {
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gray-400);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 1.35rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .layer-deep { border-left-color: var(--teal); }

  .layer-tag {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--fs-micro);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gray-600);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .layer-deep .layer-tag { color: var(--teal-deep); }
  .layer h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .layer p { margin: 0; }

  .rail-legend {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--gray-600);
    margin-bottom: 2.5rem;
  }
  .dot {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    margin-right: 0.55rem;
    vertical-align: 0;
  }
  .dot-visible { background: var(--white); border: 1.5px solid var(--gray-400); }
  .dot-seam { background: var(--teal-tint); border: 1.5px dashed var(--teal); }

  .evidence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.9fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .evidence h2 { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
  .evidence .lede { margin-bottom: 1.15rem; }

  .evidence-panel {
    background: var(--navy-800);
    border: 1px solid var(--navy-700);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    padding: 2rem;
  }
  .evidence-panel h3 {
    font-size: var(--fs-micro);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.13em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .source-list { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .source-list li {
    padding-block: 0.9rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line-dark);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .source-list li:first-child { border-top: none; padding-top: 0; }
  .source-list strong {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--white);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .source-list span { font-size: 0.84rem; color: var(--gray-400); line-height: 1.55; }

  .cta-band { background: var(--gray-100); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .cta-inner { text-align: center; max-width: 44rem; }
  .cta-device {
    width: 180px;
    margin: 0 auto 1.75rem;
    color: var(--teal);
  }
  .cta-inner h2 { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .cta-inner .lede { margin-bottom: 2rem; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .spine, .evidence { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
